INT. CHURCH BELL TOWER - SNIPER NEST - DAY

Broken stone. Bells long gone. A sandbag parapet at the slit window. Dust hangs in the shafts of light. Distant shelling.

SERGEANT AMADOU DIALLO (40s, helmet, three days of beard) lies prone behind a rifle. Eyes fixed on a far street.

PRIVATE KAZIMIERZ "KAZ" NOWAK (19, spotter, binoculars, cracked lips) crouches beside him with a field radio.

KAZ
Movement. Window, third floor.

DIALLO
Which building?

KAZ
Blue shutters.

DIALLO
Got it.

A mortar thuds close. Grit rains from the vault. Neither flinches.

KAZ
(into radio)
Echo Two to Base. Contact.

Static. Nothing.

DIALLO
They can't hear you.

KAZ
(muttering)
Come on, come on.

Diallo shifts the rifle. Exhales. Waits.

KAZ (CONT'D)
(down the stairwell, shouting)
Hold the door! Anyone comes up, you hold the door!

Silence. A boot scuffs below. Diallo glances back. Kaz nods, shrugs.

DIALLO
Count.

KAZ
Four. Five. Six.

DIALLO
Shutters.

KAZ
Opening.

A shape in the window. Diallo's finger tenses on the trigger. A pause. A breath.

DIALLO
(to himself)
Not yet.

KAZ
Sarge.

DIALLO
Not yet.

The shape retreats. The shutters close. Diallo lets his shoulders drop one inch.

KAZ
They're playing with us.

DIALLO
We play back.

He resettles. Kaz lifts the binoculars. The shelling picks up again.

CUT TO BLACK.
